# SEO SOVEREIGNTY: INFINITY PROTOCOL v8.4.0

> Consolidates `seo_governance.mdc`. One rule, absolute authority.

## 1. NEXT.JS METADATA API (App Router)

Every public-facing page MUST export a strongly-typed `generateMetadata` function.

```typescript
// ✅ REQUIRED: Strict Metadata Generation
import { Metadata } from 'next';
import { getProductById } from '@/lib/db/products';

type Props = { params: { slug: string } };

export async function generateMetadata({ params }: Props): Promise<Metadata> {
  const product = await getProductById(params.slug);
  const baseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL || 'http://localhost:3000';

  if (!product) return { title: 'Not Found' };

  return {
    title: `${product.name} | Premium Brand`,
    description: product.description.slice(0, 160),
    alternates: {
      canonical: `${baseUrl}/products/${params.slug}`,
    },
    openGraph: {
      title: product.name,
      description: product.description.slice(0, 160),
      url: `${baseUrl}/products/${params.slug}`,
      siteName: 'Premium Brand',
      images: [
        {
          url: product.imageUrl || `${baseUrl}/og-default.png`,
          width: 1200,
          height: 630,
          alt: product.name,
        },
      ],
      locale: 'en_US',
      type: 'website',
    },
    twitter: {
      card: 'summary_large_image',
      title: product.name,
      description: product.description.slice(0, 160),
      images: [product.imageUrl || `${baseUrl}/og-default.png`],
    },
  };
}
```

## 2. DYNAMIC SITEMAP MANDATE (`app/sitemap.ts`)

Hardcoded XML sitemaps are forbidden. All Next.js projects MUST dynamically generate sitemaps using Server Components.

```typescript
// ✅ REQUIRED: Dynamic Sitemap Generation (app/sitemap.ts)
import { MetadataRoute } from 'next';
import { getAllProducts } from '@/lib/db/products';

export default async function sitemap(): Promise<MetadataRoute.Sitemap> {
  const baseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL || 'https://domain.com';
  
  // Fetch dynamic routes
  const products = await getAllProducts();
  const productEntries: MetadataRoute.Sitemap = products.map((product) => ({
    url: `${baseUrl}/products/${product.slug}`,
    lastModified: product.metadata.updatedAt.toDate(),
    changeFrequency: 'weekly',
    priority: 0.8,
  }));

  // Static routes
  const staticEntries: MetadataRoute.Sitemap = [
    { url: baseUrl, lastModified: new Date(), changeFrequency: 'daily', priority: 1.0 },
    { url: `${baseUrl}/about`, lastModified: new Date(), changeFrequency: 'monthly', priority: 0.5 },
  ];

  return [...staticEntries, ...productEntries];
}
```

## 3. ROBOTS MANDATE (`app/robots.ts`)

```typescript
// ✅ REQUIRED: Dynamic Robots (app/robots.ts)
import { MetadataRoute } from 'next';

export default function robots(): MetadataRoute.Robots {
  const baseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL || 'https://domain.com';
  
  return {
    rules: {
      userAgent: '*',
      allow: '/',
      disallow: ['/admin/', '/api/', '/_debug/', '/tmp/'],
    },
    sitemap: `${baseUrl}/sitemap.xml`,
  };
}
```

## 4. SCHEMA.ORG (schema-dts)
- Use `schema-dts` for all structured data. No raw JSON-LD strings.
- Required schemas: `Organization` (root layout), `Product` (commerce), `Article` (blog), `BreadcrumbList` (navigation).

```tsx
// ✅ REQUIRED: Type-Safe JSON-LD Component (components/seo/JsonLd.tsx)
import { Thing, WithContext } from 'schema-dts';

export function JsonLd<T extends Thing>({ schema }: { schema: WithContext<T> }) {
  return (
    <script
      type="application/ld+json"
      dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: JSON.stringify(schema) }}
    />
  );
}

// Usage in page.tsx:
// <JsonLd<Product> schema={{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Product', name: '...' }} />
```

## 5. IMAGE SEO & VITAL METRICS
- ALL `<img>` → `next/image` with `alt`, `width`, `height`.
- WebP/AVIF format mandatory.
- Preload hero images via `priority={true}` prop.
- **Core Web Vitals Budget**: LCP < 2.5s, CLS < 0.1, INP < 200ms. Non-negotiable.

